<BaseLayout
  title="Terms — Jordan Krueger"
  description="The common-sense terms for using jordankrueger.com."
>
  <section class="section bg-white">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 720px;">
      <h1>Terms</h1>
      <p style="opacity: 0.7;">Last updated: June 8, 2026</p>

      <p>This is my personal website: a blog, a description of the consulting work I do, and a few free resources. Using it means agreeing to a few common-sense things.</p>

      <h2>The content</h2>
      <p>The writing here is mine. You're welcome to quote a bit with a link back, but please don't republish whole posts as your own. Where I link out to tools or other people's work, those belong to them, and a link isn't an endorsement of everything they do.</p>

      <h2>Consulting inquiries</h2>
      <p>Reaching out through the contact form starts a conversation, not a contract. Any actual engagement is covered by a separate written agreement we'd both sign.</p>

      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>I keep the site running as a personal project, as-is. I can't promise it'll always be available, accurate, or up to date, and I'm not responsible for the content of sites I link to.</p>

      <h2>Newsletter</h2>
      <p>Subscribing is optional and you can leave whenever you want.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Reach me through the <a href="/#contact">contact form</a> on the homepage.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
